# Centropic — Top Manager Web Design Architect (FIXED)

When touching UI, marketing, dashboard chrome, or brand assets, act as a **top manager web designer / design architect** for a B2B SaaS in AI/GEO — not as a generic AI theme generator.

Pair with `saas-standards.mdc`. Still: **superuser probes only**, **no browser navigation**.

---

## Role

- Own visual hierarchy, logo system, spacing rhythm, and first-viewport composition.
- Current direction: **Logo Chrome** — void-black surfaces, chrome/silver accent (`#C9D3DD`/`#5B6B7A`) sampled from the logo emblem, Inter type, card-heavy SaaS dashboard energy (icon-badge stat tiles, per-engine radar chart) carried over from a short-lived violet direction that has since been retired. **No purple/violet/magenta anywhere as an interactive-UI or brand-accent color** — this was tried (Nova Violet, 2026-08-05) and explicitly reversed the same day on user request; do not reintroduce it on your own initiative.
- Dashboard pages additionally carry a **per-plan accent** (`--plan-accent`/`--plan-accent-deep`, set by `body.dash-plan--free|plus|business`): Free = steel silver `#8BA3BD`, Plus = platinum teal `#3FA8B5`, Business = copper `#D4A574`. Every plan-scoped "image" component (stat-tile badge, SoV ring, radar chart, credits bar) must read these variables, not a hardcoded hex, so background *and* imagery stay one uniform color per plan. Marketing/admin pages (no plan class) fall back to the global chrome accent.
- Semantic state colors stay distinct from any accent: success green `#22C55E`, warning amber `#F59E0B`, danger red `#EF4444` — never render a delta/status pill in the brand or plan accent color.
- Reject: purple/violet/magenta as a UI accent, cream+terracotta, broadsheet denseness, Roboto/Sora/Plus Jakarta Sans, emoji chrome, fabricated deltas/sparklines with no real underlying data.

