## Logo system (source of truth)

| Asset | Use |
|---|---|
| `static/img/logo.svg` | **Primary mark**, true self-contained vector (polygon/ellipse/path + inline gradients, zero external refs) — header, hero, overlays, page-intros, auth. Edit this to change the mark. |
| `static/img/logo-mark.svg` | Compact vector mark ≤28px (sidebar) — simplified geometry, same style. |
| `static/favicon.svg` | Same compact-mark design. |
| `static/img/logo.png` / `logo-mark.png` / `apple-touch-icon.png` / `favicon-32.png` / `favicon-16.png` | Raster renders of the SVGs (`cairosvg`) — only for contexts that require raster: apple-touch-icon, JSON-LD `logo`/`image`, `<link rel="icon" sizes="any">` fallback. |
| `static/img/og-share.jpg` | Social only (1200×630). |

The landing hero background is now CSS-only (dark diagonal wash + chrome radial glow + void-black gradient, see `.hero-visual--cite` in `app.css`) — the old `hero-cosmic.jpg` photoreal 3D emblem backdrop was removed 2026-08-06 (same banned-pattern reason as the raster logo below). Don't reintroduce a photo/raster emblem behind the hero.

**Two banned patterns for this mark, both tried and reverted the same day (2026-08-05):**
1. *Photoreal 3D raster as "the logo"* — looked good large, unusable crisp at favicon/sidebar sizes.
2. *SVG wrapping that raster via `<image href="other.png">`* to avoid touching templates — browsers treat an SVG loaded via `<img src="...">` as a restricted "image context", and the internal `<image>` reference to an external raster did not reliably paint, so the logo went blank everywhere.

The current mark is a genuine flat/gradient vector (no external refs) — safe to reference directly via `<img src="....svg">` in every browser, and scales cleanly from a 16px favicon to a 220px auth-page render (both verified). Don't reintroduce either banned pattern.

Rules:
1. Wordmark on `#hero-brand` (landing hero only) is **`CENTROPIC.AI`, uppercase, chrome-gradient text** (`background-clip: text`). Everywhere else the brand row keeps the plain lowercase `centropic.ai` wordmark — do not let the dramatic hero treatment leak onto other pages' brand rows again; it visually overwrote those pages' own H1 (fixed 2026-08-05, see `#hero-brand .hero-brand-word` scoping in `app.css`).
2. Brand must win the first marketing viewport over the headline (size/weight/order) — but only on the actual hero; on every other page the page's own H1 stays the visual lead over the brand row above it.
3. Logo is a **stylized flat/gradient vector hex chassis** (dashed orbital ellipse + satellite node + chrome **C** monogram) — do not swap it back to a photoreal 3D raster or a generic circle-icon.
4. Nebula blue/violet atmosphere stays behind the landing hero visual only — never bleed it into buttons, links, or focus states (those use the chrome UI accent `--brand-cyan: #C9D3DD`, or the active plan's `--plan-accent` on dashboard pages).
5. Keep mark + wordmark as one lockup; no overlapping title/badge collisions.
6. Prefer `logo-mark.svg` when the full mark would muddle at small sizes.
7. To change the mark again: edit `logo.svg` and `logo-mark.svg`/`favicon.svg` directly (both are hand-authored vector shapes, not derived from a raster source), then re-render `logo.png`/`logo-mark.png`/`apple-touch-icon.png`/`favicon-*.png` from them via `cairosvg` for the raster-only contexts.
8. **Every inline `<script>` in a template must carry `nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}"`** (CSP is `script-src 'self' 'nonce-...' 'strict-dynamic'`) — an un-nonced inline script is silently dropped by the browser with no visible error, which is how the dashboard Score/SoV tab switcher went dead (2026-08-05, `templates/dashboard.html`, pre-existing since 2026-07-27). Grep `<script>` (no `nonce=`, no `src=`) before shipping any template touching `<script>` blocks.

